Replace u8"\uFFFD" with hex-escape literal to avoid GCC 16 char8_t strictness.

In C++17 `u8"..."` is `const char[]`, but GCC 16 applies C++20 `char8_t` type
even under -std=c++17, causing:

    error: conversion from 'const char8_t [4]' to non-scalar type 'const std::string' requested

The UTF-8 bytes of U+FFFD (REPLACEMENT CHARACTER) are EF BF BD — write them
directly as a plain char literal so no u8 type juggling is involved.

--- a/src/cpp/src/whisper/word_level_timestamps.cpp
+++ b/src/cpp/src/whisper/word_level_timestamps.cpp
@@ -324,7 +324,8 @@
     const std::vector<int64_t>& tokens,
     ov::genai::Tokenizer& tokenizer) {
     const std::string decoded_full = tokenizer.decode(tokens, ov::genai::skip_special_tokens(false));
-    const std::string replacement_char = u8"\uFFFD";
+    // u8"..." is char8_t[] under GCC 16 even in C++17 mode; use raw UTF-8 bytes instead.
+    const std::string replacement_char = "\xef\xbf\xbd";
 
     std::vector<std::string> words;
     std::vector<std::vector<int64_t>> word_tokens;
